# Vercel upload exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM .gitignore. When no .vercelignore is present,
# the Vercel CLI falls back to .gitignore — which already excludes `.env`. But
# that makes a security-critical property depend on a file that exists for a
# different reason and could be edited for a different reason. A single tidy-up
# of .gitignore could silently start uploading the database password. This file
# states the rule directly.
#
# `.env` holds the Supabase password, the admin password and the session secret.
# Production values live in Vercel's environment settings, never in the upload.

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local database (conda cluster, if ever placed here)
pgdata/

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
generated/
.vercel/

# Test and tooling noise
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
CLAUDE.md
